    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CRdfyw3596ixeonh52Nx8Y)_\n\n## What\n\nNew module `sp-magit-style` (`libraries/modules/prog/`, loaded right after `sp-vcontrol`), with literate doc `docs/tangles/prog/sp-magit-style.org` and a CHANGELOG entry.\n\n- `magit-section-heading`: height 1.15, bold, overline (extended across the window)\n- `magit-diff-file-heading`: slightly larger, bold\n- Folded/expanded indicators: Nerd Font chevrons via `magit-section-visibility-indicators` (work in a TTY too)\n- Icons before every file and directory via `magit-format-file-function`, using `nerd-icons-icon-for-file` / `-for-dir`. `nerd-icons` is already set up in `sp-icons`, so no new package is added.\n- Options: `sp-magit-style-icons`, `sp-magit-style-heading-height`.\n\nApplies to `M-x yadm` (`magit-status \"~/\"`) as well, since it is plain Magit.\n\n## What it looks like\n\nNo screenshot: it was not run. Expected result in the status buffer:\n\n```\n Unstaged changes (2)          <- bigger, bold, overlined\n   .config/emacs-modular/init.el\n   README.org\n```\n\n## Not tested\n\n**Nothing was tested, in Emacs or on your Mac.** The container has no Emacs, so I could not even byte-compile it. Please try `M-x load-file` on the module, then `M-x magit-status`. Things to watch: the `magit-format-file-function` argument list (written from memory of Magit 4), the chevron glyphs needing a Nerd Font, and that heading faces survive your theme.\n\nI also could not verify `bennyandresen/jujutsu.el`: fetching it needed a permission that was not granted, and a web search did not turn it up (it found `vc-jj` instead). The design is my own, not taken from it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01RiDGYrhpzsea2M9dkqZnzz)_",
